    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="6c6874f4-86fa-570a-809e-9c0985476206" activityNameId="a678a668-c772-5ad3-9950-dd9d05125cd9" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Concrete sleeper, at regional storage</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Concrete sleeper, at regional storage
The production of railway sleepers was modelled according to the information in Messmer &amp; Frischknecht (2016). These are monoblock sleepers weighing 280 kg each and measuring 30 x 23.5 x 260 cm. The data includes the production of the concrete sleepers and the transport of the materials by rail and road from Europe and Switzerland. Cuts and rejects are not taken into account.

According to the SBB, the lifespan of such a railway sleeper is 40 years. Maintenance work, renovations and the removal of sleepers are not taken into account.; UUID:9051c306-fb38-3b43-9959-0ef4a5cc9651
The inventory includes all the materials, energy and transport necessary to manifacture 1 concrete sleeper. Excluded are maintenance and disposal
Location: Data apply to construction in Switzerland. 
Technology: Average technology available on the market
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: 
Sampling: based on literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_9051c306-fb38-3b43-9959-0ef4a5cc9651.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
